%I A401205 #23 Oct 28 2026 00:11:36
%S A401205 0,2,8,32,20,38,44,68,92,74,188,140,152,146,266,164,278,170,314,536,
%T A401205 296,578,308,332,566,338,548,1274,584,614,554,668,620,674,602,716,
%U A401205 1160,722,596,1112,692,1208,1124,1220,1106,2162,1130,1436,2498,1190,1178,2156,1202,1226,1172,2186
%N A401205 Least k such that A401018(k) = n.
%C A401205 Consider the filled-empty binary column k of the fractal set described in A000360, and read V(k)={v_0,v_1,...,v_{q-1}} from the narrow top downward as in A401018, where q = A002487(k+1) and v_q=v_0. Then a(n) is the least k such that V(k) has n transitions from 0 to 1.
%C A401205 In a cyclic binary word the 0-to-1 and 1-to-0 transitions occur just as often, hence A401018(k) counts either kind of transition.
%C A401205 The sequence is well-defined since A401018(2^(2*m-1))=m, for m>=1, and A401018(0)=0.
%C A401205 Put fusc(k) = A002487(k), and let pi(d)=A020950(d)=min {k>=0:fusc(k+1)=d}. Then, for n>=1, a(n)=pi(2*n). The first column having n cyclic 0-to-1 transitions has the same index as the first occurrence of 2*n in the shifted Stern sequence. Stern showed in 1858 that fusc(k)/fusc(k+1), k>=1, enumerates the positive rational numbers without repetition. Therefore a(n) is the first index in this enumeration for which the denominator is 2*n.
%C A401205 Write c(k)=A401018(k). First occurrences in both c(k) and fusc(k+1) cannot occur at odd indices, since c(2*m+1)=c(m) and fusc(2*m+2)=fusc(m+1). For m == 0 (mod 3), m>0, we have c(2*m)=c(m-1), while for m == 2 (mod 3), c(2*m)=c(m). Apart from a(0)=0, a first occurrence at 2*m thus requires m == 1 (mod 3). The sum fusc(m) + fusc(m+1) is even under precisely the same condition, and then equals 2*c(2*m), thereby proving a(n)=pi(2*n). Furthermore, a(n) == 2 mod 6 for every n>=1.
%D A401205 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), Sur l'Effet Noah en Géométrie, rapport à l'INPI, Mars 1995.
%D A401205 B. Reznick, Regularity Properties of the Stern Enumeration of the Rationals, Journal of Integer Sequences 11 (2008), Article 08.4.1.
%D A401205 M. A. Stern, Ueber eine zahlentheoretische Funktion, J. Reine Angew. Math. 55 (1858), 193-220.
%F A401205 a(n) = min_{k>=0: A401018(k)=n} for n>=0, with a(0)=0.
%F A401205 For n>=1, a(n) = A020950(2*n) = 2*min_{m>=0: A002487(m)+A002487(m+1)=2*n}.
%e A401205 The column word V(8)={1,0,1,0} has two cyclic 0-to-1 transitions. The values A401018(0),...,A401018(7) are 0,0,1,0,1,1,1,0, so no preceding column word has two such transitions. Hence a(2)=8.
%e A401205 Equivalently, A002487(8+1)=2*2, and 4 does not occur among A002487(1),...,A002487(8).
%o A401205 (PARI)
%o A401205 s(n) = if(n < 2, n, if(n%2, s(n\2) + s(n\2 + 1), s(n\2)));
%o A401205 a(n) = {if(n == 0, return(0)); my(m = 0); while(s(m) + s(m + 1) != 2*n, m++); 2*m};
%o A401205 vector(56, n, a(n - 1))
%o A401205 (Python)
%o A401205 from itertools import count
%o A401205 from functools import reduce
%o A401205 def A401205(n):
%o A401205     if n == 0: return 0
%o A401205     m = n<<1
%o A401205     return next(filter(lambda k:sum(reduce(lambda x,y:(x[0],x[0]+x[1]) if int(y) else (x[0]+x[1],x[1]),bin(k)[-1:2:-1],(1,0)))==m,count(1)))-1 # _Chai Wah Wu_, Oct 27 2026
%Y A401205 Confer A401018 for the counts of cyclic transitions whose first occurrences are recorded here, and A020950 for the denominator first-occurrence function, of which this sequence after its initial 0 is the subsequence with even indices.
%Y A401205 Confer A000360 for the Hamming weights and topology of the Gosper-Lafitte triangle, A000361 for the binary encodings of its successive column words, and A002487 for Stern's diatomic series and the enumeration of the positive rational numbers.
%Y A401205 Confer A400888 for the contents of the quarter-turn corrected Stern vectors from the same column words, and A400889 for their divisibility ranks.
%K A401205 nonn,new
%O A401205 0,2
%A A401205 _M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas)_, Oct 17 2026
